Cell[TextData[{
 "It is known that outer product of linear dependent vectors is zero. Outer \
product is denoted by \[OuterProduct] wedge (the symbol differ from \
Mathematica\[CloseCurlyQuote]s default \\\[MediumSpace][Wedge]).  It can be \
conveniently entered as  \[EscapeKey]op\[EscapeKey], [",
 StyleBox["mnemonic: first letters of product name (o)uter (p)roduct",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 "] or one can use full command name ",
 StyleBox["OuterProduct[ ]",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 ". For example,  outer product of two random multivectors can be computed as \
follows"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"36c4fceb-3671-410b-9b58-0f93b371e219"],

