Cell[TextData[{
 "Multiplication by unit scalar is understood as the vector itself, i.e.,  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"1", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Congruent]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "1a\\equiv a", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "41198830-5bc8-4b0c-ac3c-e6bf21d0c22e"],
 ". The zero-vector has zero length. Geometrically it resembles a point-like \
entity with no orientation, and usually is  denoted in a scalar-like manner, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["0", "TB"], "\[Congruent]", "0"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "{\\bf{0}}\\equiv 0", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "498a295d-758e-4874-a5fd-c09f6db2a3b5"],
 ". The sum of equal length vectors pointing in opposite directions gives \
zero-vector, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"-", 
             StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "a+(-a)=0", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "68be7be2-d821-4bd8-9b8b-300a95821e08"],
 ".  A direct construction of geometric algebra (GA) is based on the above \
vector space axioms which then are supplemented by new algebraic axioms."
}], "Text",
