Cell["\<\
Usual multiplication sign * often will be replaced by space. This is common \
practice when working in Mathematica frontend session. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d6d60db-5ba9-4d87-b215-1c47ea0ed0a0"]
}, Closed]]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 
 CounterBox["Section"],
 ".",
 
 CounterBox["Item"],
 "\t  ",
 StyleBox["Vector coordinates",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  A general vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"a", "\[Element]"}], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2316ae50-78ec-4110-bf87-50fee1d4d120"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]", "n"], TraditionalForm]], "Input",
  ExpressionUUID->"14ffb060-148d-467a-97b7-ec399743c6c5"],
 " in an n-dimensional vector space can be written as linear combination of \
basis vectors multiplied by real scalar coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[Element]"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\alpha^i\\in", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8ef7ef14-00dc-4d89-8306-0d59471725a5"],
 "\[DoubleStruckCapitalR],  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a=\\alpha^1\\mathrm{e}_{1}+\\alpha^2\\mathrm{e}_{2}+\\dots+\\alpha^n\\\
mathrm{e}_{n}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7cfe50f8-34d7-4542-b67f-a20d2477f6ef"],
 ", i.e. consider vector algebra (also GA)  over real coefficient field. If \
the coefficients are complex numbers we have complex GA  (complex Clifford \
algebra). Then the set ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"{", 
           SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
            StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "}"}], "\[Element]"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\{\\alpha^i\\}\\in", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7f1f6744-22de-4ead-835c-e4ae437c368a"],
 "\[DoubleStruckCapitalR] of  coefficients represents the vector itself and \
is called  coordinates (aka components). In terms of coordinates the \
multiplication  of vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "a", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f3232bd5-a3e4-4059-bb91-8e206b3e8a71"],
 " by\nscalar ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|
    "boxes" -> FormBox["\[Lambda]", TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\lambda", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5683adc9-dc20-4648-97e1-2a87e4603b75"],
 ", a sum of two vectors, and a zero-vector should be understood as\n\n ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]\[Alpha]", "1"], ",", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]\[Alpha]", "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", 
             ",", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Lambda]\[Alpha]", 
              StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], "}"}], ",", "\n", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], "+", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "1"], ",", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], "+", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", "2"], ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Alpha]", 
              StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "+", 
             SuperscriptBox["\[Beta]", 
              StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], "}"}], ",", "\\[NewLine]", 
         StyleBox["0", "TB"], "\[Congruent]", "0", "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "0"}], "}"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\lambda \
a=\\{\\lambda\\alpha^1,\\lambda\\alpha^2,\\ldots,\\lambda\\alpha^n\\},\\\\\n  \
a+b=\\{\\alpha^1+\\beta^1,\\alpha^2+\\beta^2,\\ldots,\\alpha^n+\\beta^n\\},\\\
\\\n  {\\bf 0}\\bzero\\equiv 0=\\{0,0,\\ldots,0\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5052b535-fe3a-4412-ae00-95d7186c12b4"],
 "\n\nGeometrically, in GA the vector represents a single oriented object \
that can be mathematically  manipulated without introducing coordinates at \
all. Frequently one is interested in angles, projections, transformations of \
vectors with respect to other vector-space objects. Although all these \
objects and transformation in GA can be expressed through the coordinates, \
their  usage obscures geometrical interpretation and, if possible, should be \
avoided."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"368aae7f-a60a-48b8-9e95-8bb8d85ae8ce"],

