 "\t",
 StyleBox["(b) truksta piesinio\n",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "(a) In GA, the initial vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "a", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4050b1f3-eade-4d10-9ffa-0888a6a8244f"],
 " and the displaced vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "b", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f6f12c8e-0ba2-4df3-9f9d-ba5edccb97b1"],
 " are one and the same, i.e., ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "b=a", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4566ee64-3b7e-4f87-83dc-25a403b10d7b"],
 ". \n",
 StyleBox["(b) ",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a3f260ae-68a5-4cbd-a3d8-e4bd6a0a1451"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "In GA it is assumed that displaced copy of the vector represents the same \
vector as  in ",
 ButtonBox["Fig.  1",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->"fig:vecbivc"],
 " (a). Apart from the displaceable vector sometimes  it is convenient to \
introduce the radius vector, for which the starting point of arrow is fixed, \
i.e., its absolute position with respect to center of origin is specified by \
point ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"0", ",", "0", ",", "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm],
      "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\{0,0,\\ldots\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dbd377c1-49b5-428a-80e1-23cb95d5662e"],
 " in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]", "n"], TraditionalForm]], "Input",
  ExpressionUUID->"a830b9cc-2891-499a-a3be-5f484030772d"],
 ". Strictly speaking, the notion of coordinate origin is extrinsic in GA \
(and\nin geometry in general, since it  can be chosen at will), nonetheless, \
it may be convenient to introduce it in some case as shown in",
 ButtonBox["Fig.  1",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->"fig:vecbivc"],
 " (b).  By the same reason, the frame in GA is not fixed and, therefore, may \
be called a displaceable frame. From a point of view of group action the \
radius vector is an element of linear transformation group, whereas \
displaceable vectors are subjects of affine group (aka inhomogeneous linear \
group). To be precise, a radius vector is a member of the affine space, \
whereas a ",
 StyleBox["displacable",
  IgnoreSpellCheck->True],
 " vector belongs to the vector space. The vector space is the affine space \
where we have \"forgotten\" the origin. In the following, if not mentioned  \
specially, the term vector will mean the displaced vector.  ",
 StyleBox["Algebra differ from geometry that it has very special element \
named \"zero\" with the property ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "+", "0", "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a+0=a", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "220c91ae-c20c-4edc-ad4a-776cede32f41"],
 StyleBox[". The notion of origin in the geometry, therefore, emerges in the \
process of algebraization of it",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 ". \n\nSimilarly,  more complicated displaceable geometric objects may be \
introduced, for example, the bivectors (oriented planes, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  GraphicsBox[
   {Thickness[0.010638297872340425`], 
    {Thickness[0.005319148936170213], JoinForm[{"Miter", 3.25}], 
     JoinedCurveBox[{{{0, 2, 0}}}, {{{61.739099999999986`, 31.4641}, {91.6719,
       75.98709999999998}}},
      CurveClosed->{0}]}, 
    {CapForm["Butt"], JoinForm[{"Miter", 3.25}], 
     JoinedCurveBox[{{{0, 2, 0}}}, {{{1.87109, 13.655100000000003`}, {27.0672,
       51.1309}}},
      CurveClosed->{0}], 
