Cell["\<\
Displaceable and radius vectors in physics. The action of gravitational force \
at any point near the Earth surface is represented by a displaceable vector. \
A homogeneous magnetic field at any point between flat and large enough  \
poles of a magnet is represented by the displaceable bivector. Example of a \
radius vector may be the vector that represents position of a material point \
(say, on the surface of the  Earth) with respect to some fixed point (the \
Earth center or the Sun).\
\>", "Subitem",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.91023453653193*^9, 
  3.910234580137424*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cba8cd39-8412-4b5b-a377-\
2bbb26484d03"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Computational verification", "ItemParagraph",
 FontWeight->"Bold",
 FontColor->RGBColor[
  0.6, 0.4, 0.2],ExpressionUUID->"b9cd287b-6c59-4c87-aaa6-029c1b5f9b87"],

Cell["\<\
All vectors in the implementation are understood as radius vectors. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"611dc563-f0b9-4d8e-b66d-8f4c32b322d6"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

