   "SubsubitemNumbered", 
    0}},ExpressionUUID->"e5c56393-b8b2-426a-87bc-124becfe75c4"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Geometric product (aka Clifford product) is a key innovation in the GA . No \
special notation is used for this product. The geometric product (GP) is an \
analogue of matrix multiplication, i . e ., the GP of two MVs can be replaced \
by multiplication of their respective matrix representations . Since the MVs \
can be represented by matrices (see unit ",
 StyleBox["\\ref {TableOfPeriodicity1}",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ") this property allows an easy transition from the matrix to geometric \
algebra and vice versa, and therefore to employ the strong points of both \
algebras . In contrast to matrix algebra, which is connected with a \
particular coordinate system or basis, the GP allows to do all calculations \
without any reference to a particular basis. Introduction of the inner and \
outer products makes GA calculations simpler, however, they become \
indispensable if the geometric interpretation of the problem is needed."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.910248091628792*^9, 3.910248097581804*^9}, {
  3.91024814765137*^9, 
  3.9102482401555223`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20dc3d2e-b490-4cf1-b005-\
caf3812236d8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 
 CounterBox["Section"],
 ".",
 
 CounterBox["Item"],
 "\t ",
 StyleBox["Geometric product of vectors",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  The GP of two vectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "a", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6b1b0ee6-1fc2-43f1-9b44-2793a8399d55"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["b", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "b", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "aba78f45-dbf7-4867-ab38-750e82713666"],
 " is called the fundamental identity. It is defined as a sum of the inner\n\
and the outer products,  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Wedge]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "ab=a\\cdot b+a\\wedge b", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0a326d8f-aeb8-4c46-8a1e-86561e6eea79"],
 ". The GP is noncommutative, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[NotEqual]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "ab\\ne ba", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ac3a3f0b-84ad-4182-9c38-1f5811d8d2ac"],
 ". One may think that the inner and outer products come from the fundamental \
identity as symmetric and antisymmetric parts: \[LineSeparator]\
\[LineSeparator]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["b", "TI"], "+", 
             StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], ")"}], ",    ", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Wedge]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["b", "TI"], "-", 
             StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
             StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {},
      "input" -> 
     "a\\cdot b=\\frac{1}{2}\\big(ab+ba\\big),\\qquad\na\\wedge \
b=\\frac{1}{2}\\big(ab-ba\\big)", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0f8d1773-cbe0-4f7c-b39c-fff30b756df5"],
 ".\[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator]The GP connects algebraic operations with \
geometric properties related to the parallelism and perpendicularity of two \
vectors:\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], " ", "\[DoubleLongLeftRightArrow] ", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], ",    ", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], " ", "\[DoubleLongLeftRightArrow] ", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[Perpendicular]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "ab=ba\\iff a\\| b,\\qquad ab=-ba\\iff a\\perp b", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e906a129-bb76-4970-a2ff-4b0b6fdbab5c"],
 ". The  parallel vectors commute while the perpendicular vectors anti \
commute under GP."
}], "Item",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.9102349636172113`*^9, {3.910236138403373*^9, 3.910236427351281*^9}, {
   3.910239042527935*^9, 3.910239147663459*^9}, {3.910248290262356*^9, 
   3.910248408095503*^9}, {3.910248438189254*^9, 
   3.910248524234677*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"590a35b5-8ac8-4f29-a2ad-\
8816400ec36c"],

