 ".\[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator]",
 StyleBox["If the dual space ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[ScriptCapitalV]", "*"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "794d7e95-ff75-4095-8e60-b4a299f506b5"],
 StyleBox[" is introduced (instead of reciprocal frame in the same space \
\[ScriptCapitalV] ), the interpretation of relation  ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], "-1"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "g^{ij}=g_{ij}^{-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "41212cb8-564f-4a6d-a2c5-0a6a8c4d7eab"],
 StyleBox[" is different.  Indeed  the metric tensor and its inverse now \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]lives\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] in different spaces. \
Therefore the ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]}]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["j", "TI"]}], "-1"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "g^{ij}=g_{ij}^{-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "ef2ebdde-c4bd-4968-8ab1-022bdcce929e"],
 StyleBox[" relation can be understood in \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]numerical\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] sense only (since objects are in different spaces!). \
This point is often ignored in text books and leads to confusion.",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 " \n\nThe upper/lower index notation in GA is used when we want to have the \
formula written in coordinates that at the same time is coordinate \
independent, like in the tensor calculus. The square of a vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a=a_1\\mathrm{e}_{1}+a_2\\mathrm{e}_{2}+\\dots+a_n\\mathrm{e}_{n}", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2f62de67-ccd4-463a-a998-8fc26e18dd24"],
 " depends on GA signature,  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1", "2"], 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1", "2"], "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2", "2"], 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2", "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", 
         "+", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", "\[PlusMinus]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1", "2"], "\[PlusMinus]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2", "2"], "\[PlusMinus]", "\[Ellipsis]", 
         "\[PlusMinus]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "2"], ","}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> 
     "a^2=a\\cdot a=a \
a=a_1^2\\mathrm{e}_{1}^2+a_2^2\\mathrm{e}_{2}^2+\\dots+a_n^2\\mathrm{e}_{n}^2=\
\\pm a_1^2\\pm a_2^2\\pm\\dots\\pm a_n^2,", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7ab1afcc-03be-4984-8e2d-7314f4be363f"],
 " where the signs at coordinates ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c9a6d762-7309-4607-a564-f8bdb69ad9fe"],
 " are determined by signature of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubsuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"], "2"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\mathrm{e}_{i}^2", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0ca3b31a-bbe5-497d-9c11-555920390630"],
 " via metric of a particular algebra. Vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["a", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "a", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "09b1c2a3-7a2b-40bd-a2d2-a6fdedf89fba"],
 " can be expended  in a form, where scalars have upper/lower indices in both \
basis\n\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a=a^1\\mathrm{e}_{1}+a^2\\mathrm{e}_{2}+\\dots+a^n\\mathrm{e}_{n}= \
a_1\\mathrm{e}_{1}+a_2\\mathrm{e}_{2}+\\dots+a_n\\mathrm{e}_{n}", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4b2c072f-27a6-4c99-9606-c3cce8e14d50"],
 ",\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a=a_1\\mathrm{e}_{}^1+a_2\\mathrm{e}_{}^2+\\dots+a_n\\mathrm{e}_{}^n= \
a^1\\mathrm{e}_{}^1+a^2\\mathrm{e}_{}^2+\\dots+a^n\\mathrm{e}_{}^n", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "615dfd45-14f5-493f-9331-08acbf78b36d"],
 ". \n\n\[LeftFloor]e stress that operation of rising/lowering of a \
coefficient index is meaningless since the coefficient is a scalar quantity \
and can\[CloseCurlyQuote]t depend on signature.  However if we want to use \
Einstein\[CloseCurlyQuote]s summation convention (which assumes that over \
repeated upper and lower index we understand summation), then it is \
convenient to use upper indices in primary space basis and lower indices for \
coefficients for expansion in reciprocal basis:  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], LimitsPositioning -> True], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a=a^1\\mathrm{e}_{1}+a^2\\mathrm{e}_{2}+\\dots+a^n\\mathrm{e}_{n}=a^i\\\
mathrm{e}_{i}=\\sum_i  a_i\\mathrm{e}_{i}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ce7340de-5119-4f4d-bf82-a86b64dae067"],
 "  and  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "1"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], "+", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], "+", "\[Ellipsis]", "+", 
         
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], LimitsPositioning -> True], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a^1\\mathrm{e}_ {}^1+a^2\\mathrm{e}_ {}^2+\\dots+a^n\\mathrm{e}_ \
{}^n=a_i\\mathrm{e}_ {}^i=\\sum_i a^i\\mathrm{e}_ {}^i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0e497e4a-91a4-4a37-bf40-77b18923eb45"],
 ". Note, that when expansion coefficient index is in the same position (up \
or down) as in the basis vector, we are forced to write summation explicitly \
(Einstein\[CloseCurlyQuote]s summation convention don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t \
apply), whereas when they are in opposite positions, summation sign is (or \
can be) omitted (summation of course is assumed).  \[LeftFloor]hen expression \
lacks a basis vector, for example, this happens after we compute square of \
vector (in orthonormal basis)\[LineSeparator]\n  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], "2"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[CenterDot]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a^2=(a^i\\mathrm{e}_{i})\\cdot(a_j\\mathrm{e}_{}^{j})=(a^i\\mathrm{e}_{\
i})(a_j\\mathrm{e}_{}^{j})=a^i a_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fdafdfcf-a90e-4216-a035-5633fc419adc"],
 ",\n  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["a", "TI"], "\[CenterDot]", 
         StyleBox["b", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[CenterDot]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], ")"}], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
             SuperscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
              StyleBox["j", "TI"]]}], ")"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], 
         SubsuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["j", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a\\cdot b=(a^i\\mathrm{e}_{i})\\cdot(b_j\\mathrm{e}_{}^{j})=(a^i\\\
mathrm{e}_{i})(b_j\\mathrm{e}_{}^{j})=a^i b_j\\delta_i^j=a^i b_i", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ce8b91f7-c538-4aec-a023-d81aac1c80bf"],
 ", \[LineSeparator]\nthen rising/lowering of such an index in the final \
expression is forbidden (despite that both ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ec6db08d-c818-47b2-b67e-9b05275a0597"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "b_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b31f2efa-a1c2-4ca6-9e5a-265e61e0142c"],
 "  are  scalars!). The reason is that in these cases we already assumed \
IMPLICITLY (before computation) that one of the expansion coefficient was \
taken from expansion in the primary basis and the other in the reciprocal \
basis (these coefficients can be completely different if computation is \
performed in arbitrary non orthogonal basis, i.e.  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a_i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3bbc0507-41ae-4b9c-854d-e630a9e1dfce"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SuperscriptBox[
        StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
        StyleBox["i", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a^i", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "33d9dc91-9240-47b9-8c45-15959407c9f9"],
 " can differ  more than just by sign or factor as  previous example \
demonstrated). Therefore simple lowering or rising of any of them in the \
final answer will spoil  our assumption that we made before calculations were \
started. It would be like changing the game rules in the middle of game. \
Lowering  or rising index in such an expression, however, is possible and  is \
realised with the help of metric tensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["k", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["i", "TI"]}]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["k", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "a^i b_i= g_{ik}a^k b_i=g^{ki}a^ib_k", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bc551785-add9-4c26-8d33-82a3d4289a08"],
 ", which takes into account basis vector index lowering/rising (since  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
          StyleBox["i", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["g", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["i", "TI"], 
            StyleBox["k", "TI"]}]], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], 
