Cell[TextData[{
 "From the answer above we clearly see that for higher algebras grade-4 \
element appears. Therefore we could not expect the general formula to be \
correct when bivector is not blade. Therefore we change algebra  to n=3, for \
example ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e20736ee-bb81-48f3-b22c-264463e5856c"],
 " and show that for this algebra we get correct answer"
