 "\[LineSeparator]Duality scheme in geometric algebra"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"30675dae-18ac-42b2-9cb1-412147b9ad96"],

Cell[TextData[{
 " The  vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "1"], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\grade{\\m{A}}{1}", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "42c75e05-1f8d-4845-8577-3ad0385dfd04"],
 " has a dual vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
        RowBox[{
          StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", "1"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "\\grade{\\m{A}}{n-1}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cb7e1a8e-453c-4654-8d53-baad43ac953d"],
 " called pseudovector etc. In general, any MV ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\m{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b7972365-f73f-47d9-a8f2-3a0bd1e056b2"],
 " has a dual MV (aka Hodge star) denoted as   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star}\\mspace{-4mu}\\m{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "64d295e8-84d2-4924-9485-80e379f97012"],
 "\[LineSeparator]\n",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-1"], "  ", "Hodge dual"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star}\\mspace{-4mu}\\m{A}=\\m{A} I^{-1}\\quad\\text{Hodge dual}", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "696edeb8-8fbf-455c-b40b-715d07a4e090"],
 ".\[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator]Equality of binomial coefficients ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["m", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubsuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["C", "TI"], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
            StyleBox["m", "TI"]}], 
          StyleBox["n", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "C_m^n=C_{n-m}^n", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "27f501d7-8f75-4230-aed6-29c0b0adc5e1"],
 " implies that the number of linearly independent elements in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
          StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
        StyleBox["m", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\grade{\\m{A}}{m}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "490c552d-24c0-4e7f-9a90-dd8cb3cf7d6e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
            RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
              StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
          StyleBox["m", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
            StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], 
          RowBox[{
            StyleBox["n", "TI"], "-", 
            StyleBox["m", "TI"]}]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> 
     "\\grade{^{\\star}\\mspace{-4mu}\\m{A}}{m}=\\grade{\\m{A}}{n-m}", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "be839231-68ab-41b0-9594-f7f5328edf31"],
 " is the same. From this follows that, in principle,  the description of GA \
requires only half of all grades. The other half can be recovered from the \
duality property. Double application of the Hodge star returns the initial MV \
either with  plus sign (when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["p", "TI"], "+", 
         StyleBox["q", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "n=p+q", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bc8525bd-e279-463c-b01e-42ef2e0956b7"],
 " is even), or with minus sign (when ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["n", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "n", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "9b415ef1-3644-4039-aa34-b135385b66d9"],
 " is odd). This implies that Hodge star operation in general is not an \
involution (it may be written as involution in some of Clifford algebras). \n",
 StyleBox["There are multiple definitions of the Hodge star in GA literature. \
For example, some authors defines it as ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star}\\mspace{-4mu}\\m{A}=\\m{A} I", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "da6e967f-05ab-4536-9a64-09351b89998a"],
 StyleBox[" or ",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star}\\mspace{-4mu}\\m{A}=\\m{A} \\reverse{I}", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1],ExpressionUUID->
  "3510cf62-de33-42a5-9b7e-605edcb0bcf6"],
 StyleBox[". All of them differ by signs only.",
  Background->RGBColor[0.87, 0.94, 1]]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"43abd268-652f-468d-b454-bfb66764093a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Hodge star.",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " In ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bce5890f-7a56-44fb-a8fc-58ecda7d6090"],
 " the multivector dual to bivector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\e{12}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "a4c7537a-dbb6-493a-9794-35f8b99fab01"],
 " is a vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "\\e{3}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "be68dc38-9c4a-4a85-96dc-cf7129b7e14d"],
 ". Indeed, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"]}], ")"}], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], "-1"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"]}], ")"}], 
         SuperscriptBox[
          RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], 
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], 
              SubscriptBox[
               StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"]}], ")"}], "-1"], 
         "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"]}], ")"}], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"]}], ")"}], 
         "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star}\\mspace{-2mu}\\e{12}=(\\e{1}\\e{2})I^{-1}=(\\e{1}\\e{2})\n(\
\\e{1}\\e{2}\\e{3})^{-1}=(\\e{1}\\e{2})(\\e{3}\\e{2}\\e{1})=\\e{3}", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c1f4f483-e014-46cf-8e71-cc86076e385e"],
 ". Applying  the Hodge star twice we find ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SuperscriptBox["\[Null]", "\[FivePointedStar]\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], 
         SuperscriptBox["\[LongEqual]", "\[FivePointedStar]"], 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"]}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "{}^{\\star\\star}\\mspace{-2mu}\\e{12}=^{\\star}\\mspace{-6mu}\\e{3}=-\\\
e{12}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d7e93aaa-fed8-4d97-a3b1-094fea3369ce"],
 ". It means that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "24b4a97b-399b-42fa-9f1a-ea1dc8bb8841"],
 " algebra elements can be written in the following more symmetric and \
agreeable manner, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox["Cl", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], ":", "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], ",", "1", ",", "2", 
             ",", "3", ",", 
             StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], "}"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"1", ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "23"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "31"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "123"]}], "}"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}:=\\{1,\\e{1},\\e{2},\\e{3},\\Ie{1},\\Ie{2},\\Ie{3},I\\} \
=\\{1,\\e{1},\\e{2},\\e{3},\\e{23},\\e{31},\\e{12},\\e{123}\\}", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "dce90145-cc52-47b9-811b-d401d6080a57"],
 ". Different ordering  and signs of basis elements in the new basis should \
be\nnoted (lexicographical ordering is routinely used in the Handbook)."
}], "Subitem",ExpressionUUID->"e55dc030-2178-4aa1-b222-6f489073a842"],

