Cell["\<\
Short comment on the above code.  First we take corresponding grades. Then \
perform one of transformation and immediately divide answer by argument \
before transformation and cancel numerator with denominator (with Simplify). \
This yields either +1 or -1, which we replace by + or - respectively.  Note \
that since we know that answer after involution can differ only by sign we \
don\[CloseCurlyQuote]t need to find inverse of homogeneous MV (that would be \
a rather complicated task). Trick is to use ordinary division and simplify.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8ed3f3cf-a773-4c2b-9b97-4607d6062fc7"],

