Cell["\<\
The code for full multiplication is very similar. We only need to make all \
partitions of binomial conjugate operations. To this end we simply first \
generated all subsets of triangle involution with index list {1,2,3,4}. \
Mathematica output of them, however,  not in the order provided in the table \
above. Fortunately package has sorting function of basis elements. Therefore \
we make at first basis elements with generated index set, then sort them in \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]RevLex\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] order (details about \
sorting is provided in the end of this notebook). Then, again, strip head of \
basis element and keep only down index set indices. In the last step we \
correct the first element of generated list that it will correspond \
gaBinomialConjugate[ ,{0}] (identity transformation). \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5d91ce28-e4c1-4250-ad5e-b45aa3b3d75a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"allPartitionsOfFour", "=", 
  RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"gaSort", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
