Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Decomposition of unity",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  The theory of idempotents can be applied as a particular realization of \
the so-called decomposition of unity, which has interesting applications in \
various areas of mathematics, for example, in modular number systems, modular \
polynomials, spectral decomposition etc. In GA the unity (scalar) can be \
decomposed into a sum of primitive mutually annihilating idempotents which \
generate the spinor space (see ",
 StyleBox["Chap.~\\ref{spinorsMVrepresentation} in Part~3",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 "). For example, it is easy to check that the decomposition of unity in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{2}{2}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fd60ae78-d6df-40d0-8c8f-72ed732d51a9"],
 "  algebra can be written as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"1", "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "2"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "3"], "+", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "4"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "1=P_1+P_2+P_3+P_4", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "92bc45c4-2448-4a06-8500-080c306ae574"],
 ", where \[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         FormBox[
          GridBox[{{"\[Null]", 
             RowBox[{
               SubscriptBox[
                StyleBox["P", "TI"], "1"], "\[LongEqual]", 
               FractionBox["1", "2"], 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"1", "+", 
                   SubscriptBox[
                    StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "13"]}], ")"}], 
               FractionBox["1", "2"], 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                 RowBox[{"1", "+", 
                   SubscriptBox[
                    StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "24"]}], ")"}], 
               ",  ", 
