Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 
 CounterBox["Section"],
 ".",
 
 CounterBox["Item"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Minimal ideal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ".  In GA the notion of idempotent is one of tools  in   paving the way for \
a concept of spinor, an object that is very important in physics. The \
construction of spinor space, in turn, is based on the concept of ideal.\
\[LineSeparator]\nLet ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\matcal{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f27a7f19-8e69-40da-a349-56c376962d4f"],
 " be an algebra. A subset ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[Subset]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\mathcal{I}_L\\subset\\matcal{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f8c74eae-2ce9-472e-890b-ff9562e59a4f"],
 "  is said to be left ideal in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       StyleBox["A", "TI"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\matcal{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "314d00fb-d37a-437c-adf7-a802fd9b2cac"],
 " if, for all MVs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\m{A}\\in\\matcal{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b08c9811-8e2c-4d7b-848b-0dbd0a333032"],
 " and for all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["L", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "f\\in \\matcal{I}_L", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8b8b4f49-280a-4290-9bbd-df4b7053ac4d"],
 ", the relation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["L", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\m{A}f\\in\\matcal{I}_L", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f8be546f-be95-4b73-af21-10361bb7308c"],
 " holds. Simply, any element of the algebra multiplied from left by any \
element of the ideal again yields an element belonging to the ideal. \
Similarly, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[Subset]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\matcal{I}_R\\subset\\matcal{A} ", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7b782f2e-b68c-47ea-9e15-6b87c27ddcec"],
 " is said to be a right ideal for all MVs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\m{A}\\in\\matcal{A}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0984362e-9d31-4353-afb8-d39a73177ae9"],
 " and for all ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "f\\in \\matcal{I}_R", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "2e75546e-f42d-41d0-aeba-d54817880e7c"],
 ", if the relation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["f", "TI"], 
         StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "f\\m{A}\\in \\matcal{I}_R", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "60fe6d44-f76b-4255-80a3-c37c06c60a0f"],
 " holds. For example, the subset ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["I", "TI"], 
          StyleBox["R", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\matcal{I}_L=\\matcal{I}_R=\\matcal{I}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c4bc9e60-2135-4943-be0a-0ef0e7091a5a"],
 " of all even numbers is the ideal in the ring (see ",
 StyleBox["Chap.~\\ref{spinorsMVrepresentation} of Part~3",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ")  of integers, since multiplication of any integer by even number always \
return even number ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         StyleBox["n", "TI"], "\[Element]", 
         StyleBox["I", "TI"]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "n\\in\\matcal{I}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5846089b-3c7d-4413-86cd-e3d47edd0193"],
 ". If a multiplication from any side yields the same ideal, the ideal is \
called bilateral. Since multiplication of integers is commutative, the ideal \
of even numbers is bilateral by construction. In GA the left and right ideals \
generally differ. The ideal is called minimal if it does not contain any \
other ideals except itself and trivial ideal. Minimal ideals are generated by \
primitive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   ButtonBox["idempotents",
    BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
    ButtonData->"idempotents"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c7f5437a-f29a-44cd-bc60-e9c06d09db26"],
 ". More details can be found in ",
 StyleBox["Chap.~\\ref{spinorsMVrepresentation} of Part~3",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 ", where applications of minimal ideals in construction of spinors in GA and \
their matrix representation is discussed."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5b3cf270-91d5-4f32-8d27-90b82f394ec8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Matrix representation of ",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],
  FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->
  "f3064b4d-6dd1-4151-b434-e87fbd22a21c"],
 StyleBox[" ideal",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". Take primitive idempotent ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], 
          SubscriptBox["Cl", 
           RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         FractionBox["1", "2"], 
         RowBox[{"(", 
           RowBox[{"1", "+", 
             SubscriptBox[
              StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"]}], ")"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\m{P}_{\\cl{3}{0}}=\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\e{3})", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8394b8e2-dc4d-434e-bc37-364a09a87b17"],
 " and substitute unit ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", 
           OverscriptBox["1", "^"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {},
      "input" -> "(1\\rightarrow \\hat{1})", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6fe73854-ae7b-43da-8fe1-69dc356aced0"],
 " and  Pauli ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], "\[Rule]", 
           SubscriptBox[
            OverscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "^"], "3"]}], ")"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "(\\e{3}\\rightarrow \\s{3})", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b672ebce-d8e8-498a-a2d8-0dd83798440f"],
 " matrices to obtain  matrix representation of the idempotent, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             FormBox[
              GridBox[{{
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell["1", "InlineFormula"], " "}]], 
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell["0", "InlineFormula"], " "}]]}, {
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell["0", "InlineFormula"], " "}]], 
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell["0", "InlineFormula"], " "}]]}}], TraditionalForm]]],
            "]"}]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\hat{P}=\\bigl[\n\\begin{matrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{matrix}\\bigr]", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "d695f3df-6ce9-436c-bbe3-86aed806ac45"],
 ". A general ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox["Cl", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", "0"}]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\cl{3}{0}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "24d4fb30-461f-4a87-ae7d-0a56855b35c9"],
 " element can be written as a complex ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"2", "\[Cross]", "2"}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "2\\times\n2", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5111545e-c189-4030-984b-52c353848970"],
 " matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             FormBox[
              GridBox[{{
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell[
                    StyleBox["a", "TI"], "InlineFormula"], " "}]], 
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell[
                    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "InlineFormula"], " "}]]}, {
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell[
                    StyleBox["c", "TI"], "InlineFormula"], " "}]], 
                 Cell[
                  TextData[{" ", 
                    Cell[
                    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "InlineFormula"], " "}]]}}], 
              TraditionalForm]]], "]"}]}], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> 
     "\\hat{M}=\\bigl[\n\\begin{matrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{matrix}\\bigr]", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8dc4161a-02d7-4178-a104-57562dbeda0a"],
 ". Multiplication of this matrix by primitive idempotent matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       OverscriptBox[
        StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\hat{P}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "66eca4df-ea97-47d5-84a1-3a173a3423b8"],
 " yields ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{
         SubscriptBox[
          OverscriptBox[
           StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], 
          StyleBox["L", "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["M", "TI"], "^"], 
         OverscriptBox[
          StyleBox["P", "TI"], "^"], "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"[", 
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             FormBox[
              GridBox[{{
                 StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
                 StyleBox["b", "TI"]}, {
                 StyleBox["c", "TI"], 
                 StyleBox["d", "TI"]}}, 
               GridBoxAlignment -> {
                "Columns" -> {Right, {Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}}, 
               GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
                    Offset[0.]}, 
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
                   Offset[0.2], {
                    Offset[0.4]}, 
                   Offset[0.2]}}], TraditionalForm]]], "]"}], 
         RowBox[{"[", 
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             FormBox[
              
              GridBox[{{"1", "0"}, {"0", "0"}}, 
               GridBoxAlignment -> {
                "Columns" -> {Right, {Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}}, 
               GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
                    Offset[0.]}, 
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
                   Offset[0.2], {
                    Offset[0.4]}, 
                   Offset[0.2]}}], TraditionalForm]]], "]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
         
         RowBox[{"[", 
           Cell[
            BoxData[
             FormBox[
              GridBox[{{
                 StyleBox["a", "TI"], "0"}, {
                 StyleBox["c", "TI"], "0"}}, 
               GridBoxAlignment -> {
                "Columns" -> {Right, {Left}}, "Rows" -> {{Baseline}}}, 
               GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`], {
                    Offset[0.]}, 
                   Offset[0.27999999999999997`]}, "Rows" -> {
                   Offset[0.2], {
                    Offset[0.4]}, 
                   Offset[0.2]}}], TraditionalForm]]], "]"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\hat{\\matcal{I}}_L=\\hat{M}\\hat{P}=\n\
\\begin{bmatrix}a&b\\\\c&d\\end{bmatrix}\n\
\\begin{bmatrix}1&0\\\\0&0\\end{bmatrix}=\n\
\\begin{bmatrix}a&0\\\\c&0\\end{bmatrix}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "21e4185d-7640-4b1c-abde-b7315d6b31b6"],
 ".  It is evident that multiplication of arbitrary matrix from the left by \
idempotent matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       SubscriptBox[
        OverscriptBox[
         StyleBox["I", "TI"], "^"], 
        StyleBox["L", "TI"]], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\hat{\\matcal{I}}_L", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fe7f2d26-c83c-4ce8-9718-b587d67c7854"],
 " returns a new matrix with a single left-most nonzero column only, i.e., \
the left column matrices represent left ideals of GA. In unit ",
 StyleBox["\\ref{GArealIdempotentIdeal}",
  FontColor->RGBColor[1, 0, 0]],
 " we will see that the minimal left ideal then can be identified with a \
respective column spinor."
}], "Subitem",
 CellTags->
  "PrimitiveIdempcl30",ExpressionUUID->"cc10b8e6-72a2-4d03-a9b6-6070dc9a2fcf"],

