 "\[LineSeparator]\[LineSeparator] In this table the next-to-last line shows \
that the left and right contractions are related and, therefore, in principle \
it is enough to define only one of them. Formulas with contractions avoid \
some implicit assumptions, which are otherwise necessary when the equations \
are rewritten in terms of symmetric dot product. In general, however, as the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   ButtonBox["Example",
    BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
    ButtonData->"dotcontraction"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c7d6b18f-45af-4b43-ae44-e8d9eeb61bbf"],
 " shows the dot product is not the same as the contraction."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"4bb50e18-aa25-4ce4-9347-e549b39c09ae"],

