Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 
 CounterBox["Section"],
 ".",
 
 CounterBox["Item"],
 "\t",
 StyleBox["Ordering of basis elements in GA",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 ". The table of primitive idempotents lists the basis elements in the order \
of growing numbers in a blade index, exactly  as letters are listed in the \
alphabet. Sometimes different ordering of basis elements is needed.  In GA \
four main orderings of basis elements are defined: lexicographic (\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Lex\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), inverse lexicographic (\
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvLex\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), reverse lexicographic \
(\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]RevLex\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]), inverse reverse\n\
lexicographic (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvRevLex\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]). \
These orderings may be preceded by two possible corrections \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Deg\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (higher degree blades \
first) or \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvDeg\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] (higher \
degree blades last), so all in all we have  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"4", "\[CenterDot]", "3", "\[LongEqual]", "12"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> "4\\d 3=12", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "185d2ad6-92e7-48d6-9f6a-46ac26fd34b8"],
 " possible orderings of GA basis elements. We will denote the additional \
orderings as \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Deg[InvLex], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Deg[RevLex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Deg[InvRevLex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvDeg[Lex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvDeg[InvLex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvDeg[RevLex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]InvDeg[InvRevLex]\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. To \
illustrate all listed orderings, the  algebra of dimension n\\ge4 is \
required. Given two sets of indices (treated as components of abstract vector \
in the index space) ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox["\[Alpha]", "2"], "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha=\\{\\alpha_1,\\alpha_2\\dots\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "282228e6-99b2-4cc7-803a-421402558f8c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Beta]", "\[LongEqual]", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
             SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "1"], ",", 
             SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "2"], "\[Ellipsis]"}], "}"}]}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\beta=\\{\\beta_1,\\beta_2\\dots\\}", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "75f69d23-e9d1-461c-abc4-aeaf9f91012c"],
 " with their lengths (which encode the grade of the element) denoted as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       TemplateBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Alpha]"}]}, "Abs"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "|\\alpha|", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c0c4f51c-1a07-4f4f-85d7-84098a51804c"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       TemplateBox[{
         RowBox[{"\[Beta]"}]}, "Abs"], TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, 
     "input" -> "|\\beta|", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4bcab97e-a703-4189-a2c3-203835b41cad"],
 " the mentioned orderings are defined in the following way: \n",
 StyleBox["Lex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "  ordering, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", 
         SubscriptBox[">", 
          StyleBox["Lex", FontSlant -> "Plain"]], "\[Beta]"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha >_\\mathrm{Lex} \\beta", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "22ac27a6-8842-4e7a-8c53-1d344c36be41"],
 ", if in the vector difference ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "-", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Element]"}],
     TraditionalForm], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ]", "n"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"02985d10-94e4-462f-9383-ccadfdf4ab49"],
 " the  left most nonzero entry is  positive (for index set with less \
elements zeroes are inserted in the place of absent index, see\nExample \
below). An example  of Lex ordering is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1234"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "123"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "124"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "134"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "13"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "14"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "234"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "23"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "24"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "34"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "4"], ",", "1"}], "}"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\{\\e{1234}, \\e{123}, \\e{124}, \\e{12}, \\e{134}, \\e{13}, \\e{14}, \
\\e{1}, \\e{234}, \\e{23}, \\e{24}, \\e{2}, \\e{34}, \\e{3}, \\e{4}, 1\\}", 
     "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4acb1736-2e3d-441c-a96b-002bde3753eb"],
 ".\n\n",
 StyleBox["InvLex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ordering, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", 
         SubscriptBox[">", 
          StyleBox["InvLex", FontSlant -> "Plain"]], "\[Beta]"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha >_\\mathrm{InvLex} \\beta", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c6059d63-7cf0-42bb-b236-d77ea6fe4a65"],
 ", if in  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "-", "\[Beta]"}], "\[Element]"}],
     TraditionalForm], 
    SuperscriptBox["\[DoubleStruckCapitalZ]", "n"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  ExpressionUUID->"aa35e8dd-aa0b-4f54-a7a8-f7284e2455c3"],
 "  the t right most nonzero entry is  positive.  An example  of Lex ordering \
is  ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "1234"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "234"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "134"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "34"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "124"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "24"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "14"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "4"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "123"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "23"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "13"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "3"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "12"], ",", 
           SubscriptBox[
            StyleBox["e", FontSlant -> "Plain"], "2"], ",", 
           StyleBox["e", "TI"], "1", ",", "1"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm], 
     "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\{\\e{1234},\\e{234},\\e{134},\\e{34},\\e{124},\\e{24},\\e{14},\\e{4},\
\\e{123},\\e{23},\\e{13},\\e{3},\\e{12},  \\e{2}, e{1},1\\}", "state" -> 
     "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "5c7640f3-a7cf-4b2b-8aca-4d96d9f32ad7"],
 ".\n\n",
 StyleBox["RevLex",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " ordering, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   TemplateBox[<|"boxes" -> FormBox[
       RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", 
         SubscriptBox[">", 
          StyleBox["RevLex", FontSlant -> "Plain"]], "\[Beta]"}], 
       TraditionalForm], "errors" -> {}, "input" -> 
     "\\alpha >_\\mathrm{RevLex} \\beta", "state" -> "Boxes"|>,
    "TeXAssistantTemplate"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7f07bc80-dec7-40b9-82ef-f9494980c7d8"],
 ", if in   ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    FormBox[
     RowBox[{
